  "_comment": "Research lexicon for generate_albani_sermons.py (issue #31). SEED CANDIDATES, NOT A VALIDATED INSTRUMENT: every entry is 'seed' until the curator's Hausa-speaking colleague accepts it through the review sheet the generator writes (--review-sheet). Only accepted rows are to be folded back here, with status 'validated'. Edit this file, never the code, to revise the instrument.",
  "_matching": "Variants are written as the transcripts spell them; matching folds hooked letters (ɓ ɗ ƙ ƴ), apostrophe typography, q/k, doubled letters and a final -ah, so one hooked spelling also catches its unhooked twin. Hausa marks possession with a linker suffix (-n / -r: matasan, gwamnatin, tarbiyyar), so the linker forms are listed explicitly; there is no lemmatiser (issue #31: 57–63% accuracy is too noisy). Multi-word variants match consecutive words of one speaker turn. Within a category, matches never overlap and the longest wins ('yan siyasa before siyasa); categories are independent of each other.",
  "_disambiguation": "'exclude_before' drops an occurrence whose PRECEDING word is listed (sarki after 'madaukakin' is the divine epithet Allah Madaukakin Sarki, 706 times in 29 transcripts). 'ambiguous' entries keep their counts and concordance lines so the specialist can judge them, but stay OUT of every pooled statistic (theme rates, collocates, network, overlap) until validated: the unhooked text merges kasa 'to fail' with ƙasa 'country', and kwaya 'grain, seed' with ƙwaya 'pill'.",
